    <div style="line-height: 1.25;"><font style="font-weight: bold;">Chen Lichtenstein, ZIM President &amp; CEO, stated</font>, &#8220;Since assuming my role in July, my focus has been clear: to capitalize fully on current market opportunities while deploying
      the Company&#8217;s resources with discipline and efficiency. We remain committed to preserving the agility that allows us to respond quickly to changing market conditions, strengthening our competitiveness, and creating sustainable value.&#8221;</div>
    <div style="line-height: 1.25;"><br style="line-height: 1.25;">
    </div>
    <div style="line-height: 1.25;"><font style="font-weight: bold;">Sami Jubran, Chief Financial Officer, added</font>, &#8220;We delivered solid results in the second quarter and expect significantly stronger performance during the remainder of the year, as
      reflected in our guidance. This anticipated improvement would enable our Board of Directors to consider declaring a dividend to shareholders based on our third-quarter results.&#8221;</div>
